Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Matrix Product States", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ac42ce7c-e2c5-4de3-ae11-5370e3f4432c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Matrix", " ", "Product", " ", "State"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2db5377d-fb6a-4643-8405-af7d8b93081a"],
 " (MPS) writes the amplitudes of a quantum state on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ded01c28-3326-4a26-8f08-cc97f2890ead"],
 " sites as a one-dimensional chain of rank-3 tensors with rank-2 boundaries. \
The ansatz is exact when the bond dimension is large enough to capture every \
Schmidt coefficient across every cut, and it is the dominant variational \
class behind DMRG, TEBD, and time evolution of one-dimensional quantum \
systems. This tutorial walks through the MPS-specific routines that the \
paclet exposes at Tier 7: canonical forms, overlaps and norms, Schmidt \
decomposition, entanglement entropy, and bond truncation. The treatment is \
practical \[LongDash] every concept is paired with a runnable example built \
on the same six-site chain so the reader can read the numbers off the page \
and predict how each operation will reshape the next one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fc0ed747-ebd5-4120-b377-ff0738912809"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<Wolfram`TensorNetworks`\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[205]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c934c9a6-ee6d-4f43-8c9b-3fe5378d2089"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. What an MPS is", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5c5ed60c-7513-493a-bec2-0a02f557a332"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "An MPS on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3b15fae9-5aa2-467d-a5a7-d7a7a72bbe78"],
 " sites with physical dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["d", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a8187546-6b76-4b28-9cb9-24c5592d927d"],
 " and bond dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3e26579a-0a60-41bb-86b5-e1082752875b"],
 " expresses the coefficients of a state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "=", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "1"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "N"]}]], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}]], 
     SuperscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}]], "\[CenterEllipsis]", 
     SuperscriptBox["A", 
      RowBox[{"[", "N", "]"}]], 
     RowBox[{"|", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "1"], "\[CenterEllipsis]", 
      SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "N"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}]}]}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "4a23acf7-3f35-415b-8260-05893792fd34"],
 " as a contracted chain of site tensors. The bulk tensors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["A", 
    RowBox[{"[", "i", "]"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a101f2d1-1a89-44ee-833e-127b424b004a"],
 " carry three indices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "i"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "i"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "i"], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"bf9ae942-f437-4205-a4c2-5cc919936846"],
 ": a left bond, a right bond, and a physical leg. The two boundary tensors \
have only one bond and one physical leg each. The total number of parameters \
in the ansatz is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"2", "\[CenterDot]", "D", "\[CenterDot]", "d"}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"N", "-", "2"}], ")"}], "\[CenterDot]", 
     SuperscriptBox["D", "2"], "\[CenterDot]", "d"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"1d770d89-49fe-43ae-b7b6-70d96cfcd9b5"],
 " \[LongDash] linear in the chain length, instead of the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["d", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"767497af-631e-4904-9575-cc4717dd1af9"],
 " parameters of the dense wavefunction. The bond dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "33110c80-4e19-4c26-ae98-2f7e0164ccaf"],
 " controls expressiveness: every Schmidt rank across every bipartition of \
the chain is upper bounded by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6461d578-140a-4607-8a26-0e0d3d808c46"],
 ", and the ansatz is exact when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"D", "\[GreaterEqual]", 
    SuperscriptBox["d", 
     RowBox[{"\[LeftFloor]", 
      RowBox[{"N", "/", "2"}], "\[RightFloor]"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0f508bdf-3682-4775-8909-65f152e4e2df"],
 ". For one-dimensional gapped Hamiltonians, however, the Schmidt rank \
saturates at a constant ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"D", "(", "\[CurlyEpsilon]", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"da409c16-7497-4a9b-858a-cdb6c55373e3"],
 " set by the desired truncation accuracy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f8bb5bf7-32cc-44c5-89cd-bc7c0f413c96"],
 ", regardless of system size \[LongDash] this is the area law that makes MPS \
competitive for ground-state simulation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8c412636-7145-42fa-98e4-0e8c2edc4a89"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The paclet builds a random MPS via ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["RandomTensorNetwork",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/RandomTensorNetwork"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"5e622a78-6a36-4c20-a291-d454dd12a527"],
 " with the named pattern ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<MPS\>\"", "[", 
    RowBox[{"N", ",", "D", ",", "d"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d4bd2691-e655-4187-9f57-025c4dd6c8c0"],
 ". The following constructs a six-site chain with bond dimension four and \
qubit physical legs."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"66451fba-f6e9-4c8c-9ee6-c8cab7270df4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "42", "]"}], ";", 
   RowBox[{"mps", "=", 
    RowBox[{"RandomTensorNetwork", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<MPS\>\"", "[", 
      RowBox[{"6", ",", "4", ",", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
