Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The companion predicate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSCanonicalQ",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSCanonicalQ"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"6c901238-0171-4086-971f-0b3210931afe"],
 " verifies the isometry condition site by site, with a default tolerance of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", 
    RowBox[{"-", "10"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "b6f85100-3364-4b66-b8b5-e9bbae589e93"],
 " on the Frobenius distance from the identity. The same predicate accepts \
the right and mixed forms."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e57a79f7-11f4-443e-a25d-83c7dbbe5eb3"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MPSCanonicalQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"MPSCanonicalForm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"mps", ",", "\"\<Right\>\""}], "]"}], ",", "\"\<Right\>\""}], 
    "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"MPSCanonicalQ", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"MPSCanonicalForm", "[", 
      RowBox[{"mps", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Mixed\>\"", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Mixed\>\"", ",", "3"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[212]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a7726f3a-e48e-45c3-ba13-835c506dfc80"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988116334676795*^9, 3.988224846975135*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[212]=",
 CellID->313616691,ExpressionUUID->"2b0ffd9b-0f7a-4a18-b3e8-27f305d2a446"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both options ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<MaxBond\>\"", "\[Rule]", "D"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"b2015b2e-7d1e-4d05-bda2-b1cfeb9d96fb"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Tolerance\>\"", "\[Rule]", "\[Epsilon]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"122f158b-196b-4214-bade-c7681f8ed536"],
 " feed into the singular value decomposition that performs each \
canonicalization step. Asking for a left-canonical form with a smaller bond \
truncates as it canonicalizes, dropping the smallest Schmidt values at every \
cut."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ad8de52a-fa87-4254-8c3d-765c29518d99"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Dimensions", ",", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"MPSCanonicalForm", "[", 
     RowBox[{"mps", ",", "\"\<Left\>\"", ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<MaxBond\>\"", "\[Rule]", "2"}]}], "]"}], 
    "[", "\"\<Tensors\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[213]:=",ExpressionUUID->"cab81d8a-8a47-4106-8597-fcba9a1754e4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988116334690308*^9, 3.988224846999692*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[213]=",
 CellID->1030855899,ExpressionUUID->"4c09d37b-680f-4dfe-92b1-87bc163bbf65"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Every bond has been reduced from four down to two. The truncation happens \
SVD by SVD as the sweep proceeds: at each bond the SVD returns Schmidt values \
in descending order, the largest ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"6dffbf5b-c9fb-459d-abb6-4c696b58c108"],
 " are kept, and the remainder is dropped together with the small singular \
modes of its product with the next site. The discarded weight contributes a \
local error and the accumulated error after the full sweep is bounded by the \
sum of the discarded squared Schmidt values across all bonds, the standard \
truncation-error estimate. The same truncation can also be reached by passing \
a positive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\"\<Tolerance\>\"", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8004a638-2d0d-4eb8-8bed-feb7489f6df6"],
 ": singular values below the cutoff are dropped, which is the variant to use \
when you want a relative accuracy target rather than a hard bond cap. The two \
cutoffs compose \[LongDash] if both are set, the algorithm keeps at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\"\<MaxBond\>\"", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c3e34af1-4877-4f90-bb67-248cf2e4c853"],
 " singular values and additionally drops any below ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\"\<Tolerance\>\"", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"98a3d6a7-583f-48b1-8d64-5459a1b2da76"],
 ", whichever is more aggressive at the given bond."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"977de5e5-fa38-452e-86a2-61adf28c4421"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Overlap and norm", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5d18327e-616d-4666-8e97-d94f8a2ae0e2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Overlaps are the workhorse subroutine of nearly every MPS algorithm: \
expectation values of local operators, energies in DMRG, fidelities in \
compression, and infidelity estimates in TEBD all reduce to inner products of \
two MPS. The inner product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", "1"], "|", 
    SubscriptBox["\[Psi]", "2"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"cc0386ff-4c64-453a-8aef-f12955dec63e"],
 " between two MPS is computed by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSOverlap",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSOverlap"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"d4dbb3f0-c2bb-447a-989c-f5d010aaf7c6"],
 ". The second argument is conjugated, matching the bra convention. The \
implementation contracts the two chains side-by-side, sweeping a \
transfer-matrix from left to right; the cost grows linearly in the chain \
length and as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["D", "3"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0a1a8115-9712-419d-98d1-35a436b7f279"],
 " in the bond dimension. The transfer matrix at site ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["i", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "98c50501-03c6-47ba-839e-d18f090df3ab"],
 " is the partial contraction of the chains over the physical leg and the \
left bond, leaving the right bond open. The sweep multiplies these transfer \
matrices in sequence and the final scalar is the overlap. Self-overlap \
returns the squared norm."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"90bfd1c9-f94a-4cda-a4d3-33b7c8edbbd4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MPSOverlap", "[", 
    RowBox[{"mps", ",", "mps"}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"MPSNorm", "[", "mps", "]"}]}], "}"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[214]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d20c89d2-50ce-438f-b39d-cb4058741d70"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"69.34374125852828`", ",", "8.327288950104247`"}], "}"}]], "Output",\

 CellChangeTimes->{3.988116334710532*^9, 3.9882248470224943`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[214]=",
 CellID->1844514144,ExpressionUUID->"9a45fa97-2196-4851-9ef7-db3685b916af"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two numbers satisfy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
     "\[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]", "\[Psi]", "\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]"}], 
     "2"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[LeftAngleBracket]", "\[Psi]", "|", "\[Psi]", 
     "\[RightAngleBracket]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2c2142de-b512-4586-87c8-ceae19bb2812"],
 ", because ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSNorm",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSNorm"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f92a2815-4c3d-464e-8752-a74e01ddd1b4"],
 " is defined as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{"MPSOverlap", "[", 
      RowBox[{"mps", ",", "mps"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2bccdbae-77f3-47a5-b226-6bfe39df528b"],
 ". To rescale a state to unit norm without rebuilding it from scratch use ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSNormalize",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSNormalize"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"8a264a5f-c7ac-4c59-b87d-4aef5087e422"],
 ", which divides each site tensor by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
    "\[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]", "\[Psi]", "\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]"}], 
    RowBox[{"1", "/", "N"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"199c3e44-5afe-4b19-bd51-e335dc43fdb3"],
 " so that the global norm is one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ff6a6bf-837a-4c91-ae00-bfc3cd436a2a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"nmps", "=", 
   RowBox[{"MPSNormalize", "[", "mps", "]"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"MPSNorm", "[", "nmps", "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[215]:=",ExpressionUUID->"9736732d-1103-41f5-b2f6-5c23f92712b1"],

Cell[BoxData["1.`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9881163347327414`*^9, 3.9882248470451183`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[216]=",
 CellID->1822773763,ExpressionUUID->"5b80c8bf-5e05-4df4-9888-aa68a12b2af0"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Normalization is effectively idempotent: a second application changes \
nothing up to floating-point error. Distributing the rescaling factor across \
every site instead of dumping it on the first tensor keeps the matrix \
elements of each site small, which avoids overflow in long chains and keeps \
later overlaps numerically well-conditioned. Normalizing before computing \
Schmidt values or entanglement entropy keeps the probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["p", "i"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d6c0ad35-05b1-4630-a4ff-a279e8555b24"],
 " on the unit simplex without per-call rescaling. Note that the overlap \
implementation never expands the chains into their dense ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["d", "N"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5dc45a3e-f265-425c-9e1e-77dcab61915c"],
 "-element vectors \[LongDash] for the six-site qubit chain above the dense \
state has 64 amplitudes, but the transfer-matrix sweep evaluates a chain of \
contractions whose intermediate sizes are at most ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["D", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d41da27b-8fa1-4d68-b9a0-50b96cf64aa7"],
 " = 16. This is the reason MPS arithmetic stays tractable when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["N", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "2022095e-0176-4af7-81b4-0462fdc10609"],
 " is large."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1a39b2ae-dc54-4882-8872-1040f2450994"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Schmidt decomposition and entanglement entropy", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2814c104-2d01-4251-bc5c-8e6c4d550042"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Splitting the chain across a bond at site ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "f82e8d08-3092-4685-89c8-6c0b4b3bb25d"],
 " realizes a Schmidt decomposition: there is a basis of left states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", 
    SubscriptBox["L", "i"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2914ecf6-d85a-41f9-88a2-24c0ab7f9c5a"],
 " on sites ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"1", "\[Ellipsis]", "k"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"fa9cadb2-4cea-4789-86e3-c327ef7ecb7f"],
 " and right states ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"|", 
    SubscriptBox["R", "i"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"dc1279ff-8ed8-43d1-8650-5d96a9e1d464"],
 " on sites ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"k", "+", "1"}], "\[Ellipsis]", "N"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0801f6db-e03d-4c0d-bd69-04d2d97465e6"],
 " such that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[Psi]", "=", 
    UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     RowBox[{"i", "=", "1"}], "r"], 
    SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "i"], 
    RowBox[{"|", 
     SubscriptBox["L", "i"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
    RowBox[{"|", 
     SubscriptBox["R", "i"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c225def4-ca3c-457f-91a8-7acb5f6431e7"],
 " with the Schmidt values ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "i"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"d87aa798-1702-4718-bd63-55d11038a0a1"],
 " non-negative and the partial probabilities ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["p", "i"], "=", 
    SuperscriptBox[
     SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "i"], "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"0a3bded3-6fe0-439e-9b2b-29d22dc47cf7"],
 " summing to one. The function ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSSchmidtValues",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSSchmidtValues"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c3ca5812-5163-4abc-a22d-089cb81c37a2"],
 " returns the normalized list."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b728bd7-d189-430f-9302-226d153bff70"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"svals", "=", 
   RowBox[{"MPSSchmidtValues", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nmps", ",", "3"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"svals", ",", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{"svals", "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[217]:=",ExpressionUUID->"20c80ffd-80a7-406c-ba2e-4cf4bd490644"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
    "0.9203449562068505`", ",", "0.3059643970354078`", ",", 
     "0.21163986127889708`", ",", "0.12066282960886993`"}], "}"}], ",", 
   "1.0000000000000002`"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988116334746079*^9, 3.988224847061615*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[218]=",
 CellID->1504410286,ExpressionUUID->"ab3cc406-280b-4bcc-ab85-2811980e5016"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Internally the function builds the mixed-canonical form centered at site ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ef897e25-2b09-46d9-944e-445f4d9a93cc"],
 ", reshapes the center tensor into the bipartition matrix, and reads the \
singular values directly. Because the Schmidt values are normalized, the list \
is exactly the bond's reduced density spectrum ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SqrtBox[
    SubscriptBox["p", "i"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"06307b6c-2a7c-4136-8ff3-b3d9c2414c9a"],
 ". The decay rate of these values across ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["i", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a7604571-b054-43f9-8797-6bb047730f06"],
 " is the fingerprint of the state's entanglement structure: an exponential \
decay indicates a state easily approximated by a small bond dimension, while \
a slow power-law decay is the signature of critical (gapless) physics that \
requires a larger ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "256d2fc9-0db2-4a87-9a3d-bdd977835a54"],
 " for the same accuracy."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ecc47c55-dc04-4332-9ee6-046ef61cac46"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The von Neumann entanglement entropy ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", "i", ""]}], 
    SubscriptBox["p", "i"], 
    RowBox[{"log", " ", 
     SubscriptBox["p", "i"]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2188e684-4dcb-4cd3-b675-048971105f96"],
 " of the same bipartition is returned by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSEntanglementEntropy",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSEntanglementEntropy"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"eefb6eca-55ae-493b-817c-d6bd258e5d5d"],
 ". For a product state at bond ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c43f554e-6ed9-40bb-8710-c09335156d45"],
 " it is zero; for a maximally entangled cut with bond dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["D", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "78fa40e7-fdab-4687-9c27-03e8b3c0796e"],
 " it is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"log", " ", "D"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"acef2743-d82a-4cc0-8afa-0e60c9b34552"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2149337e-3ab1-42b6-aaa7-49ccef82e6d6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"MPSEntanglementEntropy", "[", 
  RowBox[{"nmps", ",", "3"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[219]:=",ExpressionUUID->"da39e2e4-b7a6-4c8b-b680-9ef714496e57"],

Cell[BoxData["0.5630413824240719`"], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988116334764563*^9, 3.988224847084046*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[219]=",
 CellID->151217024,ExpressionUUID->"4e17dc7a-e08b-4a0d-8ece-65b6a7244c99"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The entanglement is below the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"log", "(", "4", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"93267ca0-1d9e-4b15-81e6-78b4f906c226"],
 " \[TildeTilde] 1.386 ceiling because the random tensors did not saturate \
every Schmidt direction. Plotting the entropy across all interior bonds gives \
the entanglement profile of the state, often called the entanglement \
spectrum's first moment."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56cc20b1-1d27-4818-beee-58282479fe0d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"MPSEntanglementEntropy", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nmps", ",", "k"}], "]"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"k", ",", "1", ",", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[220]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f82fa2df-160a-44d3-8ccd-f70f48102239"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
  "0.2010757773804715`", ",", "0.4775737501936648`", ",", 
   "0.5630413824240719`", ",", "0.6577782115030418`", ",", 
   "0.3981482398839843`"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9881163347838984`*^9, 3.9882248471066933`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[220]=",
 CellID->1031367967,ExpressionUUID->"417df9c3-9afe-4a13-89b9-6168ed3d8749"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The arch shape is typical of a finite chain: the boundary bonds carry less \
entanglement than the bulk because there are fewer sites on the short side of \
the cut, so the Schmidt rank is constrained more by the small block than by \
the bond dimension. For ground states of one-dimensional gapped Hamiltonians, \
the area law caps the bulk plateau by a constant, regardless of system size, \
which is the structural reason MPS work \[LongDash] a fixed bond dimension is \
enough to capture the entanglement of arbitrarily long chains. Critical \
(gapless) one-dimensional systems instead show ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"S", "\[Tilde]", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["c", "6"], 
     RowBox[{"log", " ", 
      RowBox[{"L", "(", "k", ")"}]}]}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"5f624896-2fbc-4a49-ab34-cd97ba3a5486"],
 ", the celebrated logarithmic CFT scaling, where ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["c", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "75f7bc78-94fb-4297-ab25-bd690b8fbd78"],
 " is the central charge of the universality class and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"L", "(", "k", ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f915c0aa-e7d0-4ee7-979b-fab66e1e1d4c"],
 " is the conformal block length of the cut. A diagnostic plot of the \
entanglement profile against ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"log", " ", "k"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0b4a70e4-4fe8-4625-ba63-f09e1477c46b"],
 " on a converged DMRG state is therefore a quick way to detect criticality \
without computing dynamical structure factors."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"04ce6079-d04a-42d5-999e-d15d5c825619"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Bond truncation and compression", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"98c4c725-a40c-44ed-a4d6-6c62a08612e4"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Variational compression of an MPS \[LongDash] reducing every bond down to a \
target dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2aefc22d-bf60-4fee-bd0f-08b635328157"],
 " while losing as little fidelity as possible \[LongDash] is exposed as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSTruncate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSTruncate"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"88043f00-5fd6-429f-b6be-16a7a5496a77"],
 ". The standard recipe is a left sweep that performs an SVD at every bond, \
keeps the top ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"490f7fe7-5bd6-4e2a-af3d-7f33e63d210c"],
 " singular values, and absorbs the remainder into the next tensor; the \
result is a left-canonical MPS by construction, optionally renormalized."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"035c1761-43a1-4cfb-a304-2842bac9248c"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"truncated", "=", 
   RowBox[{"MPSTruncate", "[", 
    RowBox[{"nmps", ",", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
  RowBox[{"Dimensions", ",", 
   RowBox[{"truncated", "[", "\"\<Tensors\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[221]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b4ffd62c-8150-427d-b767-c4acaf22fbb2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.988116334803794*^9, 3.988224847131104*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[222]=",
 CellID->1860906432,ExpressionUUID->"9eef87bf-8ce6-42f8-9700-ca76086771d5"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "The truncation cut every bond from four to two and renormalized to unit \
length (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Normalize\>\"", "\[Rule]", "True"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"90ab56c1-d89b-4ca2-821c-4ded28212f2f"],
 " is the default). The fidelity loss is the overlap between the truncated \
state and the original."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"619ecdcc-7f96-406d-97dc-3552c5e50719"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"fidelity", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
    RowBox[{"MPSOverlap", "[", 
     RowBox[{"truncated", ",", "nmps"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"fidelity", ",", 
   RowBox[{"1.0", "-", 
    RowBox[{"fidelity", "^", "2"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[223]:=",ExpressionUUID->"695e709c-966a-47cd-b683-c6ba22d814d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"0.8830551090913484`", ",", "0.2202136743076667`"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{3.9881163348243093`*^9, 3.988224847156846*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[224]=",
 CellID->302567716,ExpressionUUID->"d1e7c00d-f436-45c4-9dd4-7a8e62c3b65a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Reading off the result: the compressed state has roughly 88% projection on \
the original, and the loss in squared fidelity is about 22%%. That loss is \
the sum of the discarded ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    SubscriptBox["\[Lambda]", "i"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"25e111ee-4d84-4087-aa65-659e1f62a563"],
 " at every bond, so a tighter ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"2c68f97d-0e26-4b5c-9a6f-a57a6e81fc50"],
 " trades fidelity for storage. Strictly speaking, one sweep of left-SVD \
truncation is not the variationally optimal compression of an MPS to a target \
bond \[LongDash] the global optimum requires alternating left and right \
sweeps until convergence, since truncating bond ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["k", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9afab872-0dc1-4e0d-b5ee-c066b2b7761a"],
 " perturbs the spectrum at bond ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"k", "+", "1"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9c4e47f9-c069-4b58-8b7a-25201d6df90c"],
 ". For mildly entangled states the single sweep is usually within a few \
parts in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["10", "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"6f2d4675-0df9-4703-ac0c-40cb1bd81db0"],
 " of the optimum, which is why it is the default; for aggressive compression \
of highly entangled states an explicit variational sweep is recommended. In \
practice an MPS algorithm chooses ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["D", "max"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"8cf2d2bc-d237-4b8c-bd33-33b50ac4a84e"],
 " adaptively from the discarded weight at each bond, and the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\"\<Tolerance\>\"", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"f47263f8-c209-4a8c-8312-c980b4ac1616"],
 " option carried through to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSCanonicalForm",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSCanonicalForm"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"483d59a1-9f93-4e75-98c1-81c122e7461a"],
 " serves that role. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  ButtonBox["MPSTruncate",
   BaseStyle->"Link",
   ButtonData->"paclet:Wolfram/TensorNetworks/ref/MPSTruncate"]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"c9bd695d-469a-428a-b81f-6b705fc18fdf"],
 " is the standard variational primitive behind one-site DMRG, TDVP \
compression and the cleanup step of TEBD; in each of those algorithms the \
truncated state is the starting point for the next local optimization, so a \
left-canonical output is convenient because the local update at site one \
needs no further isometric preparation. Setting ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\"\<Normalize\>\"", "\[Rule]", "False"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"4d6cc8de-7ce9-4298-9487-213629fee865"],
 " preserves the original norm; this is the right call inside iterative \
schemes that track the norm explicitly and would double-count a rescaling."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.988116499542206*^9},ExpressionUUID->"3e5e7e15-785c-4327-9238-\
a2037c4d78a1"]
}, Open  ]],

